{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the maximum value of the expression \\(\\sqrt{c(b - c)} + \\sqrt{c(a - c)}\\) given the constraints \\(a \\ge b \\ge c \\ge 0\\) and \\(a + b = 16\\), we will proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, let's express \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in terms of \\(c\\). Since \\(a + b = 16\\), we can write \\(b = 16 - a\\). Substituting this into the expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{c(b - c)} + \\sqrt{c(a - c)} = \\sqrt{c(16 - a - c)} + \\sqrt{c(a - c)}.\n\\]\nLet \\(x = a - c\\) and \\(y = 16 - a - c\\). Notice that \\(a = x + c\\) and \\(b = 16 - x - c\\). Therefore, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{c(16 - 2c - x)} + \\sqrt{c(x)}.\n\\]\nSince \\(a \\ge b \\ge c\\), we have \\(x \\ge 0\\) and \\(16 - x - c \\ge c\\), which simplifies to \\(x \\le 8 - 2c\\). Also, since \\(a + b = 16\\), we have \\(x + c + 16 - x - c = 16\\), which is always true.\n\n","prefix_end":782,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,7192,897,315,279,7493,1124,11520,26888,90,66,1883,481,272,9139,488,1124,26888,90,66,2877,481,272,9139,57758,2661,279,16982,17767,64,1124,709,293,1124,709,272,1124,709,220,15,57758,323,17767,64,488,293,284,220,16,21,59,701,582,686,10354,3019,553,3019,382,5338,11,1077,594,3158,17767,64,57758,323,17767,65,57758,304,3793,315,17767,66,59,568,8704,17767,64,488,293,284,220,16,21,59,701,582,646,3270,17767,65,284,220,16,21,481,264,59,568,3719,3696,10607,419,1119,279,7493,11,582,633,510,59,9640,59,26888,90,66,1883,481,272,9139,488,1124,26888,90,66,2877,481,272,9139,284,1124,26888,90,66,7,16,21,481,264,481,272,9139,488,1124,26888,90,66,2877,481,272,9139,624,59,921,10061,17767,87,284,264,481,272,57758,323,17767,88,284,220,16,21,481,264,481,272,59,568,24742,429,17767,64,284,856,488,272,57758,323,17767,65,284,220,16,21,481,856,481,272,59,568,15277,11,279,7493,9044,510,59,9640,59,26888,90,66,7,16,21,481,220,17,66,481,856,9139,4